cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite it as below."
title: "Does AI rate through the cycle? — reproducibility artifact"
abstract: >
  Reproducibility artifact (code, frozen data, analysis outputs) for the first
  controlled measurement of procyclicality in credit assessment.
  Firm fundamentals are held byte-identical across an ordered macroeconomic-severity
  axis; the analysis regenerates the cyclicality coefficient, its confidence
  intervals, the asymmetry, the ordered-probit null, and the instruction contrasts
  from a frozen 32,000-rating dataset.
